yes well you heard the Home Secretary  there telling the House of Commons a  short time ago that it was what she  described as a multi-agency response but  that response had actually involved some  private fishing vessels and we have  heard now firsthand account of a skipper  of a fishing vessel by the name of  Raymond who's told Sky News that the  first he was one of the first on scene  and the first he knew of the fact that  there were people in distress was he  heard screaming around his boat it  actually woke him up he said and some of  the extraordinary footage he shared with  us shows him and his crew pulling some  30 to 40 migrants out of the water he  said that they were from all over the  world in fact he said Afghanistan Iraq  Senegal India and they all told them  that they'd paid 5 000 pounds to a  people Smuggler in France for passage to  the UK Raymond said that these people  were all given hot or well he described  them actually as lukewarm showers on his  fishing vessel and then brought him to  land where they were then uh looked over  by border Force officials and given  medical assistance but all of them he  said survived I think the most striking  thing though when you see that footage  you just played some of it if you want  to if you missed that watching at home  you can go and look at on the Sky News  website is the sheer unseaworthiness of  the vessel they are in it is it looks  like a paddling pool that is slowly  deflating in icy cold Waters as people  frantically try and Scrabble out of it  to safety and sadly that is the business  model that so many of these people  traffickers use they're putting people  clearly at risk we know fatally now with  four lives lost overnight in  spectacularly unseaworthy vessels and  it's left to people like Raymond the  Border force and others to pull them out
 

